 "text": "Hello, how are things going? You can use a grocery bag open at the top and sit on it with one hand, or buy a grocery cart that turns it into an easy to mount rack. A basket goes on the front wheel and pushes down on it, so it feels rough and scares dogs. Stick to grocery bag or get a cart. That's smart. Keep a few small bags of only basics at the house so you never have to empty the bag off the door. Not usually, but it push the load forward and down so it's hard to keep steady. Keep it on the rear rack and fill it only half way up the house.",
